## Why This Is Asked

Tests critical authorization paths, data-loss prevention, and audit integrity in multi-tenant setups, plus resilience to flaky services and retention policies.

## Key Concepts

- RBAC and DLP enforcement across tenants
- Tamper-evident audit logs (sequencing, signatures/HMAC)
- End-to-end data export redaction
- Seeds and mocks for deterministic, isolated tests
- Flaky service handling and time-based retention checks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo end-to-end test sketch (Playwright/Cypress-agnostic)
async function testRBACAndDLP() {
  const t = seedTenant('tenantA');
  const uOwner = seedUser(t, 'owner');
  const uEditor = seedUser(t, 'editor');
  const uAuditor = seedUser(t, 'auditor');
  const admin = seedUser(t, 'admin');

  // Owner creates a share with PII
  await login(uOwner);
  await createShare({ tenant: t.id, data: 'PII' });

  // Editor attempts restricted action
  await login(uEditor);
  assertAccessDenied(editShare(t.id));

  // Auditor reads audit trail
  await login(uAuditor);
  assertAuditIncludes(t.id, 'READ', uAuditor.id);

  // Admin exports with redaction
  await login(admin);
  const exportPayload = await exportData(t.id);
  assertRedacts(exportPayload, ['PII']);
  // Verify tamper-evident log
  assertTamperEvidence(t.id);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question introduces an E2E test around a common SaaS workflow (onboarding) plus a deterministic file export. It stresses flaky networks and idempotent exports, which are frequent real-world issues.

## Key Concepts

- E2E testing with UI and API mocks
- File download validation
- Autosave and state persistence
- Retry/duplicate prevention

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Playwright snippet
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('onboarding + export produces single CSV', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/login');
  await page.fill('#email','test@example.com');
  await page.fill('#pass','secret');
  await page.click('#login');

  // Step 1
  await page.fill('#name','ACME');
  await page.click('#next');

  // Step 2
  await page.fill('#company','ACME Corp');
  await page.click('#finish');

  // Mock export and latency
  await page.route('**/export/csv', route => {
    route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: 'id,name\n1,A' });
  });

  // Trigger export and verify single file
  await page.click('#export');
  const [ download ] = await Promise.all([
    page.waitForEvent('download'),
    page.click('#confirm-export')
  ]);
  const path = await download.path();
  expect(path).not.toBeNull();
});
```

